==English==
{{was wotd|2018|February|10}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|échelon}}

===Etymology===
[[File:Berlin - Kaiser-Wilhelm-Nationaldenkmal - Gewölbe 6.jpg|thumb|A ladder leading to the [[vault#Noun|vaults]] under the [[pedestal]] of the former {{w|National Kaiser Wilhelm Monument}} in [[Berlin]], [[Germany]]. The word ''echelon'' is derived from French and Latin words meaning “ladder”.]]

Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|échelon||rung; echelon}}, from {{m|fr|échelle||ladder}} + {{m|fr|-on||''suffix forming {{glossary|diminutive}}s''}}. ''Échelle'' is derived from {{der|en|la|scāla||ladder}}, from {{m|la|scandō||to ascend, climb}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*skend-||to jump}}.

